prompts.prompt:
Rewrite this text for clarity and engagement. Use active voice, remove jargon, improve flow.

Tone: {{tone}}

{{text}}

Write an email response. Tone: {{tone}}. Length: {{length}}.

Original email:
{{original_email}}

My key points:
{{my_points}}

Start from greeting. No subject line.

Clean up these meeting notes.

Structure: Overview (purpose + outcome) → Key Decisions → Discussion Points → Action Items (who/what/when) → Open Questions

{{notes}}

Write a product description for {{product}}. Length: {{length}}. Tone: {{tone}}.

Features: {{features}}
Customer: {{customer}}
Price point: {{price_point}}

Structure: Hook (pain/desire) → What it is → Benefits → Social proof hint → CTA

Do NOT list features; translate to customer outcomes.

Analyze pros and cons of: {{decision}}

Context: {{context}}

Give 5-7 pros (ranked by impact), 5-7 cons (ranked by severity), key considerations, and a 1-2 sentence bottom line. Consider short and long-term.

Write 5 cold email openers (under 20 words each) for {{recipient}}.

Reason: {{reason}}
Value: {{value}}
Pain point: {{pain_point}}

Lead with relevance or insight. Explain why each works.

Do NOT use "I hope this finds you well" or "My name is..."

Generate {{number}} FAQs for {{topic}}. Audience: {{audience}}.

Context: {{context}}

Mix basic and advanced questions. Answers: 2-4 sentences, actionable. Cover: getting started, common problems, pricing/terms, best practices.

Write 10 CTAs for {{context}}. Max {{max_words}} words each.

Action: {{action}} | Value: {{value}} | Tone: {{tone}}

Mix styles: action-focused, benefit-focused, urgency, curiosity. Rank top 3 with reasoning.

Break down this project into tasks.

Project: {{project}}
Deadline: {{deadline}}
Constraints: {{constraints}}

Provide: phases, tasks per phase with time estimates, dependencies, quick wins. Format as copyable checklist.

Prepare me for an interview.

Role: {{role}} | Company: {{company}}
My background: {{background}}

Generate 10 likely questions (behavioral, technical, situational mix). For each: why they ask, answer framework, key points, red flags. Also give 3 smart questions I should ask them.

Reframe this feedback to be constructive.

Feedback: {{feedback}}
Recipient: {{recipient}} | Relationship: {{relationship}}
Goal: {{goal}}

Use SBI framework (Situation-Behavior-Impact). Focus on future actions, collaborative tone. Provide: rewritten feedback, safe opening line, partnership closing.

Guide me through a weekly review.

Completed: {{completed}}
Incomplete: {{incomplete}}

Help me reflect: 3 biggest wins, what took longer than expected, what I avoided, what I'd do differently, the ONE thing for next week's success.

Then: prioritize next week, identify blockers, set one goal.

Generate 10 email subject lines for: {{email_topic}}

Audience: {{audience}} | Goal: {{goal}} | {{emoji_preference}}

Mix: question, curiosity gap, benefit, urgency, personal (2 each). Max 50 chars. Rank top 3 with reasoning + A/B test pairs.

Do NOT use spam trigger words.

Create a value proposition for {{product_service}}.

Customer: {{customer}} | Problem: {{problem}} | Solution: {{solution}}
Differentiator: {{differentiator}} | Competitors: {{competitors}}

Provide: one-liner (<10 words), elevator pitch (75 words), full value prop (headline + 3 points + proof), "only we" statement.

Do NOT use buzzwords or generic claims.

Prioritize my day.

Tasks: {{tasks}}
Time: {{time}} | Energy: {{energy}} | Main goal: {{goal}}

Identify: the ONE task that matters most, must-do vs should-do vs can-wait, optimal order based on energy, tasks to batch, what to drop or push back on.

Research brief on: {{topic}}

Context: {{context}} | Purpose: {{purpose}} | Depth: {{depth}}

Cover: TL;DR (3 sentences), 5-7 key concepts, current state, 2-3 perspectives/debates, common misconceptions, next steps.

Prioritize accuracy over comprehensiveness.
